WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.229 --> 00:00:02.510
(upbeat music)

00:00:02.510 --> 00:00:03.770
- [Narrator] It's one
of the biggest lockdowns

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:06.010
China has imposed during the pandemic.

00:00:06.010 --> 00:00:07.780
One that looks a lot like what happened

00:00:07.780 --> 00:00:11.930
in Wuhan two years ago when
COVID-19 first emerged.

00:00:11.930 --> 00:00:14.230
Since late December, 13 million people

00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:17.050
in the city of Xi'an have
been ordered to stay home

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:18.860
as a Delta variant led to an outbreak

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:22.510
of more than 2000 cases,
a high number for China.

00:00:22.510 --> 00:00:24.650
- They're not letting people
in or out of the city,

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:29.000
really taking just a
very aggressive approach.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:29.930
- [Narrator] China has locked down

00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:31.900
a number of cities during the pandemic,

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:34.510
and in early January
reported its first case

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:36.340
of the fast spreading Omicron variant

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:38.440
in the city of Tianjin.

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:40.000
But this time, what's happening and Xi'an

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.580
has sparked a nationwide outcry
online about food shortages.

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:46.780
Some stranded residents
said on social media

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:50.420
that they were down to their
last pack of instant noodles.

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:53.450
But the government says there
are enough food supplies,

00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:55.420
and the lockdown is
Xi'an could also threaten

00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:57.460
the global semiconductor shortage,

00:00:57.460 --> 00:00:59.130
especially since the city is home

00:00:59.130 --> 00:01:01.801
to some of the world's
biggest memory chip makers.

00:01:01.801 --> 00:01:04.240
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:05.640
The stakes are high as China

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:07.760
is about to host the Winter Olympics.

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:11.180
And the lockdown is Xi'an is
turning out to be a big test

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:13.313
for China's Zero-COVID Strategy.

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:17.550
So how strict is the lockdown in Xi'an?

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:19.250
When the rules first came into effect,

00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:21.960
one person per household
was allowed to go out

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:25.020
once every two days to buy
food and other necessities.

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:27.430
But restrictions were
tightened after a few days,

00:01:27.430 --> 00:01:29.760
with tens of thousands
send to quarantine centers,

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:31.830
and everyone else banned
from leaving their homes

00:01:31.830 --> 00:01:33.680
except to get a COVID test,

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:36.460
similar to the rules
in Wuhan back in 2020.

00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:37.400
- [Jonathan] Certainly a lot of people

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:39.880
are making the comparison
between Wuhan and Xi'an

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:42.450
and we've seen as in Wuhan two years ago,

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:46.410
we see stories coming out
through social media primarily

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:49.030
of families, households, people,

00:01:49.030 --> 00:01:52.040
encountering pretty
difficult circumstances.

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:53.650
- [Narrator] The government
promised free delivery

00:01:53.650 --> 00:01:55.850
of groceries to those stranded at home.

00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:57.720
The many complained online saying

00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:00.060
they received little to no supplies.

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:01.910
The #Xi'anGroceryShoppingIsDifficult,

00:02:03.010 --> 00:02:05.130
was viewed more than 400 million times

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:09.210
on the Chinese social media
platform Weibo as of January 7th

00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:11.390
and some say the
government hasn't provided

00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:13.501
enough food since the lockdown began.

00:02:13.501 --> 00:02:15.888
(gentle music)

00:02:15.888 --> 00:02:18.760
(indistinct chatter)

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:20.300
There were also complaints about run-ins

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:22.400
with authorities enforcing the rules.

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:24.200
This video, which has been widely shared

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:27.370
since New Year's Eve, shows
a man being beaten by guards,

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:29.070
with comments saying that he had gone out

00:02:29.070 --> 00:02:30.690
to buy steamed buns.

00:02:30.690 --> 00:02:32.500
The owner of the video couldn't be reached

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:34.980
and it hasn't been independently verified.

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:37.560
The police acknowledged the
incident and said the two guards

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:41.023
had been punished with a seven
day detention and a $30 fine.

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:44.780
Hospitals have been also widely criticized

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:47.210
on social media for
not giving medical care

00:02:47.210 --> 00:02:49.880
to some patients with
non COVID conditions.

00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:51.570
For instance, a pregnant woman said

00:02:51.570 --> 00:02:53.180
she was denied medical attention

00:02:53.180 --> 00:02:55.470
because of an expired COVID test.

00:02:55.470 --> 00:02:58.394
Authorities later said they
will loosen some requirements.

00:02:58.394 --> 00:02:59.940
- But then, there are definitely people

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:02.780
who both within Xi'an and outside of Xi'an

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:05.000
are supportive of these measures.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:07.327
People who look at the Chinese
government response and say,

00:03:07.327 --> 00:03:09.247
"That was the right thing to do."

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:11.900
- [Narrator] The lockdown is Xi'an

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:13.940
could also exacerbate the global shortage

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:17.440
of semiconductors found in the
electronics we use every day.

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:18.710
Samsung and Micron are some

00:03:18.710 --> 00:03:20.370
of the world's largest chip makers

00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:22.530
and both have factories in Xi'an.

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:24.230
According to research from TrendForce

00:03:24.230 --> 00:03:26.500
Samsung has two production
lines in the city

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:28.280
that make flash memory products,

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:31.020
used in devices such as
hard drives and cameras.

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:32.450
Samsung didn't give details,

00:03:32.450 --> 00:03:35.440
but said it had to
temporarily adjust operations.

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:37.910
Micron said the city's
closure had some impact

00:03:37.910 --> 00:03:39.310
on its output of chips,

00:03:39.310 --> 00:03:42.170
but it was working with
officials to identify solutions.

00:03:42.170 --> 00:03:43.990
- If they need to make an adjustment

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:47.600
to their Xi'an operations
that may mean that affects

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:49.870
some of their other chip
operations elsewhere.

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:52.270
We'll have to see how big
of a hit this will be.

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:55.610
- [Narrator] Just weeks
before China is set to host

00:03:55.610 --> 00:03:57.350
the Winter Olympics in Beijing,

00:03:57.350 --> 00:03:59.860
health authorities confirm
the first cases of Omicron

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:02.040
in the neighboring city of Tianjin.

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:05.130
And they ordered mass testing
for its 14 million residents.

00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:06.310
- You have officials everywhere,

00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:07.830
who are looking at Xi'an's example

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:10.830
and who are going to be hoping
that they are not subjected

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:12.421
to the same sort of scrutiny.

00:04:12.421 --> 00:04:15.200
(speaking in foreign language)

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:16.060
- [Narrator] The winter Olympics

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:18.170
is set to begin on February 4th,

00:04:18.170 --> 00:04:20.870
and China is allowing foreigners
to enter in large numbers

00:04:20.870 --> 00:04:23.100
for the first time since
the pandemic began,

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:24.930
though under very strict rules,

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:27.300
to minimize contact with locals.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:29.640
With cold temperatures
increasing transmissibility

00:04:29.640 --> 00:04:31.080
and countries around the world

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:34.020
reporting hundreds of
thousands of daily cases,

00:04:34.020 --> 00:04:37.120
keeping out COVID-19, is
becoming more challenging.

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:40.430
- China already is
feeling a lot of pressure

00:04:40.430 --> 00:04:43.250
to really pull off these
Olympics and make them succeed.

00:04:43.250 --> 00:04:45.700
There's obviously also a
lot of geopolitical pressure

00:04:45.700 --> 00:04:48.450
on China right now and so,
I think the best answer

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:49.597
that they wanna have is to say,

00:04:49.597 --> 00:04:51.540
"We pulled off a successful Olympic"

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:54.195
and part of that includes
containing COVID.

00:04:54.195 --> 00:04:57.028
(people cheering)

